    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

    <div class="faq">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Do I need a permit for window graphics in Rotterdam Centrum?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Rotterdam Centrum falls largely under welstand zone-1 &mdash; the municipality&rsquo;s strictest aesthetic tier. Films covering more than 30% of a window, and applications in protected streets such as Witte de Withstraat, may need prior municipal approval. Small logo stickers under 0.5 m&sup2; are generally permit-free. We assess each project free of charge before quoting.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Can you install window graphics in Lijnbaan or Beurstraverse?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Yes. Both centres operate tenant guides governing logo size, colour and positioning. We design to those specifications and prepare approval documentation for centre management. Share your tenant guide and we handle the paperwork.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Can I get temporary campaign film near Markthal?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Yes. For pop-up shops and seasonal promotions we use repositionable vinyl that removes cleanly without residue. For historic buildings we conduct a free pre-survey to confirm suitability before any application.</div>
